      "title": "The Turkey Illusion and Black Swans",
      "prompt": "The turkey fed for 1,000 days believes humans exist solely to serve it, right until Thanksgiving Day. Where in your strategic plan are you mistaking past stability for future safety? Where does an absence of evidence of failure mask catastrophic tail risk?",
      "placeholder": "Isolate the strategic assumption relying entirely on backward-looking data without accounting for structural shifts..."
